From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: explorer: taskbar colour, the desktops' pager, and the Rounded look

David wants the taskbar of newer Windows and the Windows 10 one mixable:
"whether or not to show the virtual desktops ... the panel a whitish blue
color like Windows 11, or black like Windows 10, or any hybrid". Settings >
Personalization > Taskbar writes, and the bar reads on "TraySettings":

- Software\Stained Glass\Taskbar Color: 0 follows the Windows mode (as
  before), 1 dark, 2 light, 3 light blue -- the whitish, faintly blue bar --
  4 the accent colour, darkened (text white).
- Software\Stained Glass\Taskbar ShowDesktops: 0 hides the virtual desktops'
  pager beside the notification area (its room goes to the buttons).
- The Rounded style (Software\Stained Glass\Style Rounded, 0483) gives the
  bar newer Windows' look: 48 px tall with 24 px icons, a rounded plate
  under the pointer and the foreground window instead of a filled button, a
  pill at a running program's foot (wide, in the accent colour, for the one
  in front), a rounded search box; its light mode is the light blue bar. The
  bar takes its new height when the style changes ("ImmersiveColorSet").

Gate: test/taskbar-gate.sh (the pager, each colour, the 48 px bar, the pill).
